    "extraction_status": "ready_for_resolution",
    "extraction_notes": "The final row of the table on document page 73 is a full-width, rule-bounded cell carrying only note text ('Note: Patients in food effect sub-study …'). It is not an activity (§4) and is emitted as one table-scope footnote with the synthesised marker 'n1', anchored to schedule_property row 1 with method 'synthesized'; per §6 the synthesised marker is deliberately NOT written onto any element's annotation_markers because the note has no modelled element to attach to. Footnotes 12 and 13 (page 73) repeat verbatim the text of footnotes 1 and 2 (page 72) under new marker numbers; both are kept because both markers are printed on the header cells. The Abbreviations block printed on both pages was not emitted (§6): none of its terms appears as a marker in a grid cell, header cell or activity label."
  },
  "table_metadata": {
    "table_number": 2,
    "table_type": "track",
    "table_title": "Table 8 Schedule of Events – Open-Label Food Effect Sub-Study (Study Completed)",
    "table_purpose": "Schedule of events for the open-label food effect sub-study: screening, the 14-day food effect period (FE Day 1 and FE Day 8), Cycle 1 and Cycle 2 visits, subsequent cycles and treatment discontinuation.",
    "track_label": "Food Effect Sub-Study",
    "page_start": 72,
    "page_end": 73,
    "notes": "Typed 'track', not 'domain' or 'subsidiary': it schedules a mutually exclusive sub-study population ('Patients in food effect sub-study …'), on its own timeline with its own columns (a 14-Day Food Effect period with FE Day 1 / FE Day 8 that does not exist in the main-study table). One logical table printed on document pages 72 and 73; page 73 repeats the title with '(Continued)' and reprints the three header rows, which are de-duplicated here. Leading label columns L=1, so the first data column is position 2 and the table has 8 data columns (2-9). Header rows 1 and 2 have an empty label cell; both property_names are synthesised. Header row 1 cells for Screening (col 2), 14-Day Food Effect (cols 3-4), Subsequent Cycles (col 8) and Treatment Discontinuation (col 9) are merged vertically through header row 2; the schema has no vertical merge, so those row-2 cells are recorded empty. The same header cells carry footnote markers 1 and 2 on page 72 and 12 and 13 on page 73, so both marker sets are recorded on the de-duplicated header cells. Cell boundaries recovered from 200-dpi raster rule-line detection (§1d); text from the pdftotext -bbox text layer."
  },
